.TH GLYD 1 "" "Glyd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glyd \- LLM weights and KV cache compressed without loss, the engine that runs them, and file compression
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glyd
.I COMMAND
[ARGS]
.br
.B glyd
[OPTIONS] [INPUT] [\-o OUTPUT]
.SH DESCRIPTION
With a command, glyd runs, serves and manages language models on Glyd's own engine. With a file and no command it compresses or decompresses the file (glyd \-\-help lists the options).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B glyd run MODEL[:LEVEL]
Chat with a model in the terminal and at one URL.
.br
MODEL is a short name (gemma4, qwen3.8:27b), a Hub id (ORG/NAME), a directory or a GGUF file. LEVEL is penguin (lossless, the default), kestrel, linnet, wren or hummingbird. \-\-prompt TEXT answers once and exits. Where the service is running the chat goes through it.
.br
Flags: \-\-context N, \-\-users N, \-\-devices LIST, \-\-port N, \-\-host ADDRESS
.TP
.B glyd serve MODEL[:LEVEL]
The OpenAI\-compatible API and the chat page.
.br
Also the Anthropic and Ollama request shapes (docs/serve\-api.md). GLYD_API_KEY, in the environment, guards /v1.
.br
Flags: \-\-context N, \-\-users N, \-\-devices LIST, \-\-port N, \-\-host ADDRESS
.TP
.B glyd pull MODEL[:LEVEL]
Download a model by name or Hub id.
.br
The level's pre\-packed repo where there is one, else the release's own weights, which the first run packs. Downloads resume and run in parallel; a gated model says where to accept its licence and to run glyd login.
.TP
.B glyd ls
The models downloaded, with their level and size on disk.
.br
The packed copies made for this GPU are totalled below.
.br
Flags: \-\-json, \-\-all
.TP
.B glyd rm MODEL[:LEVEL]
Take a model out of the cache, and its packed copies.
.br
A name with no level takes every level of the model. No other model's files are touched.
.TP
.B glyd ps
What the background service holds, and when each model unloads.
.br

.br
Flags: \-\-json, \-\-port N
.TP
.B glyd stop MODEL | \-\-all
Unload a model from the service now.
.br
The service stays. glyd service stop ends the service itself.
.br
Flags: \-\-all, \-\-port N
.TP
.B glyd service [install | uninstall | status | stop]
The background service: models load on request and unload when idle.
.br
With no word it runs in the foreground; install makes it a user unit started at login (systemd, launchd; on Windows a scheduled task of the user's, at logon). docs/service.md.
.br
Flags: \-\-port N, \-\-host ADDRESS, \-\-keep\-alive TIME, \-\-max\-loaded N, \-\-context N, \-\-users N, \-\-json
.TP
.B glyd fit MODEL[:LEVEL]
What a run would do on this computer, before anything is downloaded.
.br
The level, where the weights go, the context and the predicted tokens a second. \-\-machine plans for another computer.
.br
Flags: \-\-context N, \-\-users N, \-\-devices LIST, \-\-machine NAME|FILE, \-\-json
.TP
.B glyd doctor [\-\-bundle [FILE]] [\-\-no\-logs]
What this computer has for running models, each check with the line that fixes it.
.br
\-\-bundle writes the same as one file to attach to an issue.
.br
Flags: \-\-machine NAME|FILE, \-\-json
.TP
.B glyd names [update]
The model names (gemma4, qwen3.8:27b, ...) and their Hub repos; update fetches the latest release's.
.br
A name that is not known is looked up once a day in the latest release's manifest (GLYD_NO_REFRESH=1 stops that); the fetched file is checked against the sha256 the release lists.
.br
Flags: \-\-json
.TP
.B glyd login
Save a Hugging Face token (for a gated model).
.br
The token is kept in the Hub client's own file.
.TP
.B glyd supports MODEL
Whether the engine runs a model, from its config alone.
.br
Exit 0 it does, 3 it does not.
.br
Flags: \-\-json
.TP
.B glyd preflight [MODEL[:LEVEL]]
Whether the engine will certainly run a model on this computer, before a download.
.br
Exit 0 it will, 3 it will not (and why), 1 that could not be told.
.br
Flags: \-\-context N, \-\-users N, \-\-json
.TP
.B glyd prepare MODEL[:LEVEL]
Download a model and pack it for this GPU.
.br
Any model the engine runs, at the level glyd run would load it at (the one given, else the one that fits this computer).
.br
Flags: \-\-context N
.TP
.B glyd costs MODEL[:LEVEL] [\-\-predict]
A model's cost profile and predicted decode speed.
.br
docs/cost\-profile.md.
.br
Flags: \-\-context N
.TP
.B glyd rates [\-\-dir DIR]
This computer's memory tiers, measured.
.br
The GPU's memory, the link to it, the main memory and the disk under DIR.
.TP
.B glyd bench MODEL[:LEVEL] [\-\-suite gate|bar|full]
The benchmark harness: fixed prompts at fixed concurrencies, the speed as JSON.
.br
docs/bench.md. \-\-compare BASE CAND is the regression gate; \-\-bar is the speed bar of a GPU.
.br
Flags: \-\-context N, \-\-users N, \-\-machine NAME|FILE, \-\-json
.TP
.B glyd connect [TOOL]
What to give a program so that it talks to the server on this computer.
.br
Lines to paste for the OpenAI SDKs, Claude Code, Ollama's clients, Open WebUI, Continue and curl; nothing is changed.
.TP
.B glyd verify MODEL | PATH
Check a model's packed weights bit for bit.
.br
A model name is the engine's; a file or directory of packed weights is glyd\-gpu's.
.TP
.B glyd pack MODEL OUT
A model's weights for Glyd's GPU layouts, packed on the CPU.
.br
glyd\-gpu's command.
.TP
.B glyd cluster
One model across computers (not yet: ROADMAP.md, M4).
.br
Today that is the starlings program.
.SH SHARED FLAGS
The same flag means the same wherever a command takes it.
.TP
.B \-\-context N
the context window in tokens
.TP
.B \-\-users N
how many users the server holds at once
.TP
.B \-\-devices LIST
the GPUs to use, as the driver numbers them (0,1)
.TP
.B \-\-machine NAME|FILE
plan for another computer: a preset (rtx4080s, h100, ...) or a JSON file, not the one this runs on
.TP
.B \-\-json
the answer as JSON on the standard output, for a program to read
.TP
.B \-\-port N
the port (a port in use is an error, not a move, where it is the service's)
.TP
.B \-\-host ADDRESS
the address to listen on (127.0.0.1 unless said; another address opens it to the network)
.TP
.B \-\-all
everything, not only what is downloaded or loaded
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-alive TIME
how long an idle model stays loaded: 90s, 5m, 2h, 0, never
.TP
.B \-\-max\-loaded N
how many models the service holds at once
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
done
.TP
.B 1
an error
.TP
.B 3
not supported (glyd supports MODEL: the engine does not run it)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GLYD_API_KEY
The API key that guards /v1 of glyd serve and the service.
.TP
.B GLYD_CACHE
Where packed models are kept.
.TP
.B HF_TOKEN
A Hugging Face token.
.TP
.B GLYD_ENGINE
0 keeps vLLM, 1 uses the engine on any GPU it runs on.
.TP
.B GLYD_SERVICE_PORT
The service's port, for glyd ps, stop and run.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/surya-koritala/Glyd
